<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 December, from 537 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">537 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,489 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian dedicates Hagia Sophia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Justinian dedicated the new church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, built in under six years. It was the world's largest cathedral for nearly a thousand years and later served as a mosque and a museum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Zwickau prophets arrive in Wittenberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three men of the Radical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, exiled from Zwickau, arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>, where their ideas won favour with Andreas Karlstadt and others. The unrest that followed brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> back from protective custody at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a> in March 1522.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1655">1655 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">371 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Swedes lift their siege of the Jasna Góra Monastery</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With their position in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesser-poland">Lesser Poland</a> deteriorating, the Swedish invaders lifted their siege of the Pauline monastery of Jasna Góra in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czestochowa">Częstochowa</a>, home of the Black Madonna icon. The defence galvanised Polish resistance and made the monastery a national symbol.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jasna-gora-monastery">Jasna Góra Monastery</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-northern-war">Second Northern War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1657">1657 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">369 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Residents of Flushing sign the Flushing Remonstrance</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some thirty residents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flushing-queens">Flushing</a> in New Netherland, none of them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quakers">Quakers</a>, signed a petition asking Director-General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-stuyvesant">Peter Stuyvesant</a> to exempt them from his ban on Quaker worship. It is considered a precursor of religious freedom in the Bill of Rights.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-stuyvesant">Peter Stuyvesant</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quakers">Quakers</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The schooner USS Carolina is destroyed, ending Patterson's makeshift fleet</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The destruction of the schooner USS Carolina ended Commodore Daniel Patterson's makeshift fleet, whose delaying actions contributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a>'s victory over the British at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> in 1815.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1831">1831 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">195 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Beagle sails with Charles Darwin aboard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-beagle">HMS Beagle</a> left Plymouth on a surveying voyage with the 22-year-old naturalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-darwin">Charles Darwin</a>. His observations over the five-year journey shaped his later theory of evolution.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1904">1904 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter Pan opens on the London stage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">J. M. Barrie's play Peter Pan, or the Boy Who Wouldn't Grow Up opened at the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a>. Its story of Neverland, Captain Hook and Tinker Bell became a children's classic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet special forces kill Afghanistan's leader Hafizullah Amin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As Soviet troops poured into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, commandos stormed the Tajbeg Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and killed President Amin. The decade-long war that followed cost hundreds of thousands of Afghan lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 27 December <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-i-albert"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-i-albert.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John I Albert</span><span class="tp">1459–1501</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johannes-kepler"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johannes-kepler.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johannes Kepler</span><span class="tp">1571–1630</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mirza-ghalib"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mirza-ghalib.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mirza Ghalib</span><span class="tp">1797–1869</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 27 December <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozong-of-tang"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Emperor Gaozong of Tang</span><span class="tp">628–683</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-ii-of-kiev"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sviatoslav-ii-of-kiev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sviatoslav II of Kiev</span><span class="tp">1027–1076</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-the-pious"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-the-pious.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George the Pious</span><span class="tp">1484–1543</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christine-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christine-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christine of France</span><span class="tp">1606–1663</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stephen-f-austin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stephen-f-austin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stephen F. Austin</span><span class="tp">1793–1836</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lester-b-pearson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lester-b-pearson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lester B. Pearson</span><span class="tp">1897–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hafizullah-amin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hafizullah-amin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hafizullah Amin</span><span class="tp">1929–1979</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benazir-bhutto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benazir-bhutto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benazir Bhutto</span><span class="tp">1953–2007</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
